{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":"cli","result":{"worker":{"name":"research-iso5b-7c2d","session_id":"c2b9968d-d57b-4588-8818-11f97c09aa3e","thread_id":"01a11078-c5ca-7c00-97c8-40f9b747353c","cwd":"/private/tmp/cw-iso-7c2d/work2","tier":"medium","model":"gpt-6.1-sol","effort":"medium","access":"read_only","attach":{"listener":"ws://127.0.0.1:4612","thread_id":"01a11078-c5ca-7c00-97c8-40f9b747353c","attach_command":"codex --remote ws://127.0.0.1:4612","resume_command":"codex --remote ws://127.0.0.1:4612 resume 01a11078-c5ca-7c00-97c8-40f9b747353c"},"config":{"web_search":"live"}},"turn":{"turn_id":"01a11078-c7d6-7ae1-bbf7-d8016d33a660","status":"completed","error":null},"messages":[{"type":"agent_message","item_id":"msg_0ee9ffabe3c3b91e016ac4bac2459887d287ec164cb7b8445d","phase":"final_answer","selection":"explicit_final","text":"- **EU:** Green-tea-derived L-theanine may be used in food supplements; use in other foods requires novel-food authorisation. [Finnish Food Authority](https://www.ruokavirasto.fi/en/foodstuffs/food-sector/food-ingredients-and-contents/novel-foods/establishing-novel-food-status-of-a-food/novel-food-catalogue-of-european-commission/)\n- **US FDA (GRAS):** FDA issued a \u201cno questions\u201d response to GRN 209 for specified food uses up to 250 mg/serving; this is a GRAS notification outcome, not blanket FDA approval. [FDA record](https://hfpappexternal.fda.gov/scripts/fdcc/index.cfm?id=209&set=GRASNotices)\n- **Japan:** L-theanine is listed as a designated food additive under the Food Sanitation Act. [Designated additives list](https://ffcr.or.jp/en/tenka/lists-of-additives/list-of-designated-additives.html)\n- **Australia TGA:** Theanine is a permissible active ingredient in oral listed medicines, capped at 450 mg/day, with adult-only and pregnancy/lactation warnings. [2026 determination](https://www.legislation.gov.au/F2026L00707/asmade/2026-06-11/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_5/document_5.html)\n- **Health Canada:** L-theanine has a natural health product licensing monograph for temporary relaxation in adults at 200\u2013250 mg/day; it excludes food-like dosage forms. [Health Canada monograph](https://webprod.hc-sc.gc.ca/nhpid-bdipsn/atReq?atid=l.theanine2)\n- **China NMPA:** I found no verified NMPA approval; tea-derived theanine was approved as a new food ingredient by the health authority, now NHC, under Announcement 2014 No. 15. [Official announcement](https://www.nhc.gov.cn/sps/c100088/201407/9bceee42235d4dcc934ddf3b3e580877.shtml)"}],"structured_output":null,"metrics":{"wall_duration_seconds":{"value":58.81832758296514,"source":"codex-worker","availability":"measured"},"item_counts":{"value":{"userMessage":1,"commandExecution":2,"agentMessage":2,"webSearch":14,"reasoning":3},"source":"codex-worker","availability":"derived"},"command_count":{"value":2,"source":"codex-worker","availability":"derived"},"command_duration_ms":{"value":0,"source":"codex","availability":"derived"},"token_usage":{"value":null,"source":"codex","availability":"unavailable"}},"recovery":{"status":"codex-worker status --name research-iso5b-7c2d","messages":"codex-worker messages --name research-iso5b-7c2d","interrupt":"codex-worker interrupt --name research-iso5b-7c2d","raw_resume":"codex --remote ws://127.0.0.1:4612 resume 01a11078-c5ca-7c00-97c8-40f9b747353c"}}}
